From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ysfaculty <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 12:57:55 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 162/162] hjviewer: hjv-e2e streams end once a file says the
 checks are done
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The E2E's background streams (TV-W5's S35, S34 and S38's [끄기]) have to
outlast some checks, and ran for a fixed number of seconds well past them.
With HJV_E2E_STREAM_UNTIL=<file>, --hjv-e2e-stream also ends as at its
seconds (the frames line, the close, exit 0) once that file exists, after
`hjv-e2e: released`. Such a stream waits for its messages 200 ms at a time
to look for the file between them, and still ends after 30 s without one;
its seconds stay the cap. Only in builds with the hjv-e2e feature.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
